chambers of the US Congress. But the president still has a lot of power — and the Democrats have yet to agree on how best to use theirs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's Meloni blames pro-Russian hackers for cyberattack on minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfd7d1bbf9d652acfe23475163e79ba6c235380fdb2c7f1ab6e3f92f9d66c89e</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-s-meloni-blames-pro-russian-hackers-for-cyberattack-on-minister/a-79885200--f6543501c58b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-s-meloni-blames-pro-russian-hackers-for-cyberattack-on-minister/a-79885200?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Antonio Tajani has said hackers published personal data stolen from him as Giorgia Meloni blamed pro-Russia criminals for the incident. The news follows a string of bomb threats that have grounded flights across the EU.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: 22 killed in strike near Sanaa, Houthis say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ca298b29b768114e1399d83a1a7e41fea7bc9a67149bffb4ac2639705806c50</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-22-killed-in-strike-near-sanaa-houthis-say/a-79885177--581ded90619a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-22-killed-in-strike-near-sanaa-houthis-say/a-79885177?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group accused Saudi Arabia of hitting several homes in the village of al-Shariya near the Yemeni capital. There was no initial comment from Riyadh.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New Zealand election too close to call with over 95% of votes counted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6769782f360060f1ead66a2f7e30ade8cf79cfc68519de9422e1bae582e35830</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-zealand-election-too-close-to-call-with-over-95-of-votes-counted/a-79883056--e9f880c38325.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-zealand-election-too-close-to-call-with-over-95-of-votes-counted/a-79883056?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Initial results in New Zealand show the two main parties neck-and-neck with fewer than 4,000 votes separating them. Official results aren't expected until later this month once special votes have been counted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e81b4f8057841b955832f1d576b2c5223edfea6a6f120074677f83f459c57f5</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>France braces for new round of Yellow Vest, student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46e4d8e50bf4b518883cc64b3587d4698906832113e5efc9fa4c1b654a05e162</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T10:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-braces-for-new-round-of-yellow-vest-student-protests/a-79884064--bbcdd8927e7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-braces-for-new-round-of-yellow-vest-student-protests/a-79884064?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two major protests have been announced for Saturday. One will see students and unions marching against high living costs, while the Yellow Vests plan to march separately, despite a police ban.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia hits Kyiv with airstrikes ahead of trilateral talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c18edd253b38aaf9f787d12ba49cfba5bb03512e553d6040e3094963e2ad70e9</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851--55817e315a75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The strikes hit a major bridge and energy facilities in the Kyiv region. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy accused Moscow of trying to "push" Ukraine "into a blackout" ahead of talks in Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Frankfurt braces for Iran protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cee3484d29cceb84b6903bd9b1a1592759e64570c86eba4a4c48fbc3e62a4ad</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-frankfurt-braces-for-iran-protests/live-79883533--0a769d8187c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-frankfurt-braces-for-iran-protests/live-79883533?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An appearance by Iranian opposition figure Reza Pahlavi is expected to trigger demonstrations in Frankfurt. Meanwhile, Germany's defense minister says he believes military conscription will not be needed. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Amid protests, France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c259f5c523433eb39f8531fe5703f947192493678b76d544b79d7959b854583</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--50648477f294.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US: Giant pandas from China make public debut at Atlanta zoo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f89560174a7ce83d05b9fa7b7b1105740a014adaee9c6fab932bb39c24d692f9</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-giant-pandas-from-china-make-public-debut-at-atlanta-zoo/a-79883388--b468c87ae7ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-giant-pandas-from-china-make-public-debut-at-atlanta-zoo/a-79883388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ping Ping and Fu Shuang are the first giant pandas to be housed in Zoo Atlanta after a gap of two years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Vehicles major cause of Delhi pollution, top court says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb65fc8d976252317a0142962924074d7df84f2a616576c9d0f173e0d826ea74</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T07:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-vehicles-major-cause-of-delhi-pollution-top-court-says/live-79883248--8418b6668d5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-vehicles-major-cause-of-delhi-pollution-top-court-says/live-79883248?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Supreme Court called for responsible celebrations during festivals, particularly Diwali, as it addressed the issue of air pollution in Delhi. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US asks China to uphold Busan trade deal commitments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fa87d59c31d3cd7caddef8485332d2d4e5ce82f13e401b51a80be8ddda0cb2e</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T04:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-asks-china-to-uphold-busan-trade-deal-commitments/a-79882939--7107d3b9b548.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-asks-china-to-uphold-busan-trade-deal-commitments/a-79882939?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US urged Beijing to meet commitments from a 2025 accord — particularly on agricultural purchases and rare earths supply. China, meanwhile, expressed concern over the US' "economic, trade restrictive" measures.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cornell faculty declares 'no confidence' in university leadership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a902a619131bca652356bd6457905f30525108891701072fdad3260e2a6658c</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T03:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cornell-faculty-declares-no-confidence-in-university-leadership/a-79882895--89d8cf118513.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cornell-faculty-declares-no-confidence-in-university-leadership/a-79882895?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The university leadership has faced intense criticism for its handling of sexual crimes on campus 